-- title:
--   Toric torsion as integral points reducing into the torus
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$, and let $\Lambda$ be level data for $(N_0,p,A)$: a structure morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{base}\,p$ restricting along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ to the generic point, a scheme $X$ with $f \colon X \to \mathrm{base}\,p$, a relative group law $\Lambda.L$ on $f$, and bijections from $\mathrm{JZero}\,N_0$ and from its residue-field analogue onto the sections of $f$ over the generic point and over the residue point $\mathrm{resPt}\,A$ followed by $\sigma_A$; assume $\Lambda$ satisfies the conjunction `IsJacobian` (abelian-scheme property bundle, commutativity of $\Lambda.L$, additivity and Galois equivariance of the point parametrisations, compatibility of reduction, and realisation of the Hecke algebra by endomorphisms of $f$). Let $O$ be a Néron object for $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0 p)$ at $p$ over these data, with smooth separated group scheme $g \colon G \to \mathrm{base}\,p$, group law $O.L$, parametrisation $O.\mathrm{pts}$ of $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0 p)$ by sections of $g$ over the generic point, toric rank, toric lifts and the two fibre morphisms $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$ ($i \in \{0,1\}$) between the base changes of $g$ and of $\Lambda.f$ along the residue point. Let $m > 0$ be coprime to $p$ and let $x \in \mathrm{JZero}(N_0 p)$ be killed by $m$. Then $x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the additive subgroup generated by the range of the toric points $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$, if and only if there is a section $s \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to G$ over $\sigma_A$ whose restriction along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is the section attached to $x$ by $O.\mathrm{pts}$, and such that for both $i$ the image of the restriction of $s$ to the residue point under $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$ is the identity section of $\Lambda.L$ over $\mathrm{resPt}\,A$ followed by $\sigma_A$.
--
--   This is the Néron-model criterion for toric torsion: a prime-to-$p$ torsion point of $J_0(N_0p)$ is toric exactly when it extends to an $A$-valued point of the Néron object whose reduction is annihilated by both abelian-quotient maps of the special fibre, i.e. lies in the torus. It is the characterisation used in Ribet's level-lowering argument at a prime exactly dividing the level, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.smul_sub_self_mem_toricPts_of_isGluedSpecialization`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.smul_sub_self_mem_toricPts_of_isGluedSpecialization).
